; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR STARSHIP  -  the COSMAC ELF logo, any key to quit
; ==========================================================================
; The COSMAC ELF starship logo, drawn once and left on the screen. Any key clears
; it and returns to the monitor.
;
; Each lit cell is a SPACE in reverse video (ESC[7m), which paints a solid block on
; anything that understands it, back to a real VT100. The cursor is hidden while
; the picture is up.
;
; THE ARTWORK is traced from APPLICATIONS/Cosmac Elf Starship.jpeg rather than drawn
; freehand. The photo was area-sampled to a 160x46 map - each cell the fraction of
; its patch brighter than the background - and the ship's outline measured off that,
; then halved into these 80x23 coordinates. The logo is LINE ART, not silhouette:
; the saucer, the hull and the bracket are hollow outlines, and a straight 2:1
; reduction breaks a one-stroke outline into dashes. So the ship is emitted as
; explicit runs at the measured coordinates, which keeps every line continuous and
; keeps the saucer hollow. COSMAC and ELF are set in a 5x5 block font copied from
; the photo's letterforms; sampled glyphs lose their counters at 80 columns and
; turn to mush.
;
; THE PICTURE IS A RUN TABLE, not a bitmap. A bitmap of 80x23 would be 230 bytes of
; ones and zeros that still needs unpacking bit by bit; instead every unbroken
; horizontal stretch of lit cells is stored as three bytes - line, first column,
; length - and a line byte of $00 ends the table. 107 stretches, 322 bytes, and the
; whole renderer is a dozen commands: read three bytes with READIDX, position the
; cursor, emit that many spaces, repeat.
;
; That also makes the drawing cheap to send: 1350 bytes of output for the whole image,
; because a run of twenty blocks costs the eight bytes of its position plus twenty
; spaces rather than twenty separate positions.
;
; ADDRESSES. The READIDX base in the code is PROGRAM-RELATIVE - $0900 means $4900
; at run time - but the data D-lines below carry the ABSOLUTE address. Writing the
; table at the relative address would drop it on the firmware.
;
; Any key quits: SERIN waits cooperatively, yielding to the scheduler rather than
; spinning, so other VMs keep running while the picture is up.
;
; HW-VERIFIED 2026-08-22 on the Elf2K - Craig flashed and ran it.
;
; Sim-verified: the run table replayed back into a 23x80 screen reproduces the
; artwork cell for cell (0 differences), and the keypress restores normal video,
; shows the cursor, clears the screen and homes.
;
; The picture as it appears:
;
; |                                                                                  |
; |   ##### ##### ##### #   # ##### #####                                            |
; |   #   # #   # #     ## ## #   # #   #                                            |
; |   #     #   # ##### # # # ##### #                                                |
; |   #   # #   #     # #   # #   # #   #                                            |
; |   ##### ##### ##### #   # #   # #####                                            |
; |                                                                  ########        |
; |                                        ########################################  |
; |                 ###                    ########################################  |
; |            #############              ##                                    ###  |
; |  ############         ############     ########  #############################   |
; |  ##            #####             ##           #  ##                              |
; |  ############         ############            #  ##                              |
; |             ##############     ##             #  ##                              |
; |                #####     ###### ###           #  ##         ##### #     #####    |
; |                           #####  ##           #  ##         #     #     #        |
; |                         #######################  ######     ####  #     ####     |
; |                       ####     ################  ######     #     #     #        |
; |                      ####  ###########               ##     ##### ##### #        |
; |                       ###                 #############                          |
; |                        ####       #########                                      |
; |                           #########                                              |
; |                                                                                  |
;
; 72 STELLAR commands, $4000-$4099 (154 bytes of code).
; Data at $4900, 322 bytes, past the end marker.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; D 4000 CD             START                  Start of program, and run the label pre-pass
; D 4001 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A        Ten, for splitting numbers into digits
; D 4005 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 4007 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 4009 CA 32          SEROUTI 32             2
; D 400B CA 4A          SEROUTI 4A             J - clear the screen
; D 400D CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 400F CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 4011 CA 3F          SEROUTI 3F             ?
; D 4013 CA 32          SEROUTI 32             2
; D 4015 CA 35          SEROUTI 35             5
; D 4017 CA 6C          SEROUTI 6C             l - hide the cursor
; D 4019 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 401B CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 401D CA 37          SEROUTI 37             7
; D 401F CA 6D          SEROUTI 6D             m - reverse video: a space is now a lit block
; D 4021 11 09 00 00    LOADXI R9 0000         Index into the run table
; D 4025 2E 09 09 00    READIDX R9 0900        The line this run sits on
; D 4029 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000            Zero ends the table
; D 402C A0 00 52       IFTRUEI SHOWN
; D 402F 21 0D          COPYAX 0D              into R13 for POSXY
; D 4031 42 09          INCX R9
; D 4033 2E 09 09 00    READIDX R9 0900        The column it starts at
; D 4037 21 0E          COPYAX 0E              into R14
; D 4039 42 09          INCX R9
; D 403B 2E 09 09 00    READIDX R9 0900        and how many cells long it is
; D 403F 21 0A          COPYAX 0A              into R10
; D 4041 42 09          INCX R9
; D 4043 BD 00 78       CALL POSXY
; D 4046 CA 20          SEROUTI 20             A space in reverse video is a lit block
; D 4048 43 0A          DECX R10
; D 404A 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10
; D 404C A1 00 46       IFFALSEI CELL
; D 404F B0 00 25       GAL NEXT
; D 4052 CB             SERIN                  Wait for any key - SERIN yields, so other VMs keep running
; D 4053 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 4055 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 4057 CA 30          SEROUTI 30             0
; D 4059 CA 6D          SEROUTI 6D             m - back to normal video
; D 405B CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 405D CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 405F CA 3F          SEROUTI 3F             ?
; D 4061 CA 32          SEROUTI 32             2
; D 4063 CA 35          SEROUTI 35             5
; D 4065 CA 68          SEROUTI 68             h - show the cursor again
; D 4067 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 4069 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 406B CA 32          SEROUTI 32             2
; D 406D CA 4A          SEROUTI 4A             J - clear the screen
; D 406F CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 4071 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 4073 CA 48          SEROUTI 48             H - cursor home
; D 4075 F0 00 00       BREAK                  End of program
; D 4078 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B             ESC
; D 407A CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B             [
; D 407C 4D DF          DIVXY R13 R15
; D 407E 25             COPYMAA
; D 407F 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 4082 C9             SEROUT                 Tens
; D 4083 27             COPYREMA
; D 4084 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 4087 C9             SEROUT                 Units
; D 4088 CA 3B          SEROUTI 3B             ;
; D 408A 4D EF          DIVXY R14 R15
; D 408C 25             COPYMAA
; D 408D 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 4090 C9             SEROUT                 Tens
; D 4091 27             COPYREMA
; D 4092 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 4095 C9             SEROUT                 Units
; D 4096 CA 48          SEROUTI 48             H
; D 4098 BE 00          RETURN
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; CODE  -  download this block
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

D 4000 CD
D 4001 11 0F 00 0A
D 4005 CA 1B
D 4007 CA 5B
D 4009 CA 32
D 400B CA 4A
